    "Services" : {

    },
    "Share sends the flattened image through the macOS share sheet, and Pin floats it above your windows. Dragging the file icon in the title bar hands the flattened image to another app. Nothing is uploaded: Kadr never sends a capture anywhere." : {

    },
    "Share, pin and drag" : {

    },
    "Show All" : {

    },
    "Show Inspector" : {

    },
    "Show in Finder" : {

    },
    "Space plays and pauses. J, K and L step back, stop and play; arrow keys move the playhead, ⇧-arrows trim, ⌥-arrows take larger steps. ⌘K splits at the playhead. Delete removes the selected clip or zoom, with Undo." : {

    },
    "Speech" : {

    },
    "Split Clip at Playhead" : {

    },
    "Still running: %@. Closing stops it and deletes any partly written file." : {

    },
    "Still running: %@. Closing stops them and deletes any partly written file." : {

    },
    "Stop and Close" : {

    },
    "Stop work on “%@”?" : {

    },
    "Studio" : {
      "comment" : "The video editor for screen recordings.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Studio"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The capture underneath never changes. Every arrow, shape, text box and blur is an object you can select, move, restyle or delete later, and undo goes back as far as you need. The picture is flattened only when you copy, save or share it." : {

    },
    "The editor closed before these annotations were saved." : {

    },
    "The look is in the editor’s Look list. Open a capture to apply it." : {

    },
    "The project keeps the original pixels." : {

    },
    "The studio edits a copy of the timeline, never the recorded file. Split, trim and delete clips on the timeline; add zooms that follow your clicks; crop and set a backdrop. Undo covers every change." : {

    },
    "Tools" : {

    },
    "Top Edges" : {

    },
    "Transcribe makes a transcript and captions on this Mac. Find Cuts proposes pauses and filler words to remove, and nothing is cut until you apply the proposal." : {

    },
    "Trim End to Playhead" : {

    },
    "Trim Start to Playhead" : {

    },
    "Trimming “%@”…" : {

    },
    "Undo" : {

    },
    "Vertical Centers" : {

    },
    "View" : {

    },
    "Window" : {

    },
    "You have %lld Kadr documents with unsaved changes. " : {

    },
    "Zoom" : {

    },
    "Zoom In" : {

    },
    "Zoom Out" : {

    },
    "and %lld more" : {

    },
    "⇧⌘L locks the annotations already on the canvas, so drawing over them cannot move them by accident. Commands that would change a locked object are greyed out until you unlock." : {

    },
    "⌘C copies the image as you see it, annotations included. With annotations selected, they are copied too, so pasting into another Kadr window gives editable objects. Copy without annotations is in the toolbar's Copy menu." : {

    },
    "⌘S saves beside the capture, or over it when Keep the original file is off in Settings ▸ General, and writes a .kadr project next to it so the capture stays editable. ⇧⌘S chooses a format and quality. Move to Trash removes the capture and its project together." : {

    },
    "⌘Z and ⇧⌘Z undo and redo. ⌘C copies, ⌘S saves, ⇧⌘S saves as, ⌥⌘S saves the project. ⌥⌘I shows or hides the inspector. ⌘= and ⌘- zoom the canvas, ⌘1 fits it and ⌘0 shows actual size. ⌘D duplicates the selection, Delete removes it. ` and + or - change the armed tool's size." : {

    }
  },
  "version" : "1.0"
